# Paste the credential the offline issuer logs under `200`, and NOT a token from
# your own identity provider. These requests reach the app directly on port
# 8006, which bypasses Catalyst -- so the app is verifying against whichever
# issuer it was configured with, and a token signed by anyone else is refused
# 401 oauth.invalid_signature. Under `diagrid dev run` that issuer is Catalyst,
# and nothing you can paste here will satisfy it; the credential-bearing
# requests below therefore need the offline issuer:
#
#   DIAGRID_QUICKSTART_IDENTITY=local APP_PORT=8006 go run -tags offline .
#
# The `-tags offline` is not optional. The offline issuer is compiled in by that
# build tag alone, and without it the app refuses to start rather than trusting
# tokens it minted itself.
#
# See "## Run Offline Without a Catalyst Project" in README.md. The two requests
# that send no credential at all answer 401 in either mode.
#
# Leave the placeholder unedited and the credential-bearing requests answer
# 401 {"error": "oauth.decode_error"}: the literal text below is not a
# well-formed JWT, so it is rejected before any signature check happens.
@token = <THE_CREDENTIAL_LOGGED_UNDER_200>

### Who is calling, with no credential: 401 {"error": "oauth.missing_token"}
### The middleware rejects this before the agent, the model, or any app code runs.
GET http://localhost:8006/whoami

### Who is calling, with a credential: 200 and the verified caller
### subject, tenant and issuer_id are read off the token the app verified, never
### off the request. Against real Catalyst they come from a Catalyst-signed
### identity the sidecar produced from your identity provider's token, and the
### app never sees that original; offline they come from local_identity.go.
GET http://localhost:8006/whoami
X-Diagrid-User-Token: Bearer {{token}}

### Run the agent as that user: 200
### The reply names the caller because the verified subject reached the tool as
### an argument the loop substituted, not because the tool read a header.
POST http://localhost:8006/agent/run
X-Diagrid-User-Token: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "task": "What bookings do I have?"
}

### Run the agent with no credential: 401 {"error": "oauth.missing_token"}
### Same rejection on every route. RequireAuth is app-wide, not per-path.
POST http://localhost:8006/agent/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "task": "What bookings do I have?"
}
